If an employee is selected at random from those who prefer soup, what is the probability that the employee works the morning shift?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{7}{83}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{7}{35}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{7}{23}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{16}{23}$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'C', NULL, E'This is a conditional probability question. Given that the employee prefers soup, the sample space is restricted to the $23$ soup-preferring employees. Of those, $7$ work the morning shift, so the probability is $\\frac{7}{23}$. The answer $\\frac{7}{83}$ incorrectly uses the total number of employees as the denominator instead of conditioning on soup preference. The answer $\\frac{7}{35}$ divides by the morning shift total rather than the soup total. The answer $\\frac{16}{23}$ gives the probability of an afternoon shift employee among soup-preferring employees, which answers the wrong question.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"},"C":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"misread_question"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 75, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);

































